         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Introduction\n\nIn previous classes, we learned that we cannot write a number greater than 9 in a single position. When that happens, we need a new order — a new place in the number family — to hold the number.\n\nIn this class, we look at the same idea from another angle: the complement and the limits of a position.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "a0599aa8-c642-4f1b-976a-df63dd3ea019",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "a0599aa8-c642-4f1b-976a-df63dd3ea019",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "thinking",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "cabc9843-35ef-4e4f-92fd-17eda864b55e",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=cabc9843-35ef-4e4f-92fd-17eda864b55e",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Complement of 10\n\nBefore adding two numbers, it helps to check whether the result will stay inside the limit of a position.\n\nSince a position cannot hold more than 9, we look at the complement to 10: the number we can add without passing 10.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "e2405750-4b2b-4df0-acff-87e00671cd12",
         "prev": "6298da03-29e6-4d13-9a5e-8791b934e67e",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "e2405750-4b2b-4df0-acff-87e00671cd12",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "cabc9843-35ef-4e4f-92fd-17eda864b55e",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=cabc9843-35ef-4e4f-92fd-17eda864b55e",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Ourselves\n\nLet us start with ourselves. Each hand has 5 fingers. Add 4 more and we reach 9 — still short of 10. But with 5 or more, the result reaches or passes the limit of the position, as Calculation 1 shows:",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\" style=\"background-color:#FFFFFF;\"><p class=\"center_notation\" style=\"font-size:1.6em; line-height:1.6;\">5 + 5 = 10<br />6 + 5 = 11<br />7 + 5 = 12<br />8 + 5 = 13<br />9 + 5 = 14</p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Calculation 1</b>: Adding 5 to 5, 6, 7, 8 and 9. In every case the result is 10 or more, so a new order is needed.</p></div></center>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "Vertical list of five additions: 5 + 5 = 10, 6 + 5 = 11, 7 + 5 = 12, 8 + 5 = 13 and 9 + 5 = 14.",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "eb0d4184-7d66-44e2-9742-e7c88c4780ee",
         "prev": "a0599aa8-c642-4f1b-976a-df63dd3ea019",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "eb0d4184-7d66-44e2-9742-e7c88c4780ee",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "inlove",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "cabc9843-35ef-4e4f-92fd-17eda864b55e",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=cabc9843-35ef-4e4f-92fd-17eda864b55e",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### My Complement, My Limit\n\nThe complement of a number to 10 is the number you must add to reach 10. With 6, its complement is 4, because 6 + 4 = 10.\n\nLet us draw it to make it even clearer:",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 632 56\" width=\"100%\" style=\"max-width:632px; display:block; margin:0 auto;\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Six light blue squares followed by four light yellow squares\"><title>Six light blue squares and four light yellow squares, ten in all</title><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"64\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"128\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"192\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"256\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"320\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightblue\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"384\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"448\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"512\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"576\" y=\"0\" width=\"56\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"lightyellow\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Figure 1</b>: The number 6 (blue) and its complement 4 (yellow). Together they fill the ten squares.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "Six light blue squares followed by four light yellow squares, ten in all.",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "1c35a845-e170-4a66-9be9-59f3a3cefa33",
