               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=cabc9843-35ef-4e4f-92fd-17eda864b55e",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Exercising\n\nUse the arrows to change the number added to 6 and watch when the result advances to the next order.\n\nBelow the complement, the result stays in the units order. At the complement or above it, the result advances to the next order.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "5cd14439-1ac6-4010-9b8b-56d16c976006",
         "prev": "eb0d4184-7d66-44e2-9742-e7c88c4780ee",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "5cd14439-1ac6-4010-9b8b-56d16c976006",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "thinking",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "cabc9843-35ef-4e4f-92fd-17eda864b55e",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=cabc9843-35ef-4e4f-92fd-17eda864b55e",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Let Us Think!\n\nIf a value is smaller than the complement of 10, does the column carry a number?",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "abcee086-fa78-4d5b-aea5-18a0f7b37186",
         "prev": "1c35a845-e170-4a66-9be9-59f3a3cefa33",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": "no",
         "score": 2,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "abcee086-fa78-4d5b-aea5-18a0f7b37186",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "party",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "cabc9843-35ef-4e4f-92fd-17eda864b55e",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=cabc9843-35ef-4e4f-92fd-17eda864b55e",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Conclusion\n\nIn this class, we learned that, before adding another number, we must check the complement of the first number to 10.\n\nAdd less than the complement and the column carries nothing. Add the complement or more and the column carries 1 to the next order.\n\nIn the next class, we will practice all that we have learned.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "",
